#. module: sale_exception_order_restrictions_bl
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_sale_exception_order_restrictions_bl
msgid ""
"=================================\n"
"Sale Exception Order Restrictions\n"
"=================================\n"
"\n"
".. \n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! This file is generated by oca-gen-addon-readme !!\n"
"   !! changes will be overwritten.                   !!\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! source digest: sha256:33fb666bf0f69ae834d7570692e9c0d010ee184b6d50d561f2789f1b16c87916\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"\n"
".. |badge1| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/maturity-Beta-yellow.png\n"
"    :target: https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status\n"
"    :alt: Beta\n"
".. |badge2| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/license-AGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"    :target: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0-standalone.html\n"
"    :alt: License: AGPL-3\n"
".. |badge3| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/github-baselogica--ar%2Fbaselogica--open--addons-lightgray.png?logo=github\n"
"    :target: https://github.com/baselogica-ar/baselogica-open-addons/tree/20.0/sale_exception_order_restrictions_bl\n"
"    :alt: baselogica-ar/baselogica-open-addons\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2| |badge3|\n"
"\n"
"The sales order is not confirmed while something sets it apart from the\n"
"customer's form, until it is fixed or a Sales administrator ignores its\n"
"exceptions. Each restriction is a rule of the sale exception engine:\n"
"\n"
"- **Payment terms** other than the ones of the customer's form.\n"
"- **Delivery method**: an order with goods and no delivery method, or\n"
"  with another method than the one of its delivery address or its\n"
"  company. A method where the customer collects the goods (a pickup) is\n"
"  valid for any address.\n"
"- **Customer's purchase order**: a customer marked \"Purchase Order\n"
"  Required\" needs its number in the Customer Reference.\n"
"- **Urgent order**, with the \"Urgent\" tag: a Sales administrator\n"
"  confirms it.\n"
"- **Quantity with decimals** of goods counted in units (the unit, a\n"
"  dozen, a pack), like 1.5 units: nobody ignores it, the line is fixed.\n"
"  Setting the precision of the quantities to whole numbers is not the\n"
"  same: it rounds without warning.\n"
"- **Expired quotation**: it is not confirmed with its old prices.\n"
"  \"Update Prices\", shown only on the expired quotation, brings today's\n"
"  prices with the same recalculation as changing the pricelist, today's\n"
"  date and a new expiration, and leaves the total before and after in\n"
"  the history.\n"
"- **Credit limit**, off: the order that takes the customer over its\n"
"  credit limit, as the quotation warns (what the customer owes, its\n"
"  confirmed orders to invoice and this order). The company that wants to\n"
"  stop it turns the rule on.\n"
"\n"
"Besides:\n"
"\n"
"- Only a Sales administrator ignores the exceptions or unlocks a\n"
"  confirmed order, also through the API.\n"
"- The portal and automated processes are not stopped by any rule: the\n"
"  order is confirmed with the differences in its note and an activity\n"
"  for its salesperson.\n"
"- Confirmed orders are locked for everyone.\n"
"- An order with quantities delivered or invoiced is not cancelled,\n"
"  neither from the order nor from the list: it is undone with the return\n"
"  and the credit note, and then it is cancelled.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"- On each customer that works with purchase orders: Sales & Purchase →\n"
"  Purchase Order Required (set on the company; its branches and\n"
"  addresses follow it).\n"
"- On each pickup delivery method: Customer Collects.\n"
"- The rules, in Sales → Configuration → Sales Orders → Sale Exception\n"
"  Rules: a Sales administrator turns off the ones not used with their\n"
"  Active toggle (a company that sells goods counted in units in\n"
"  fractions turns off \"Quantity with decimals\"); a Settings\n"
"  administrator makes blocking the ones nobody may ignore, and creates\n"
"  new rules with a filter.\n"
"- To stop the orders over the credit limit: Accounting → Configuration →\n"
"  Settings → Sales Credit Limit, with its Default Credit Limit, and each\n"
"  customer's own limit in its form (Credit Limits); then, in Sale\n"
"  Exception Rules, a Sales administrator turns on \"Customer over its\n"
"  credit limit\" with its Active toggle (the list shows the rules on and\n"
"  off).\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Confirm the order as usual. When it is stopped, fix what the exception\n"
"says, or a Sales administrator confirms it with \"Ignore Exceptions\".\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/baselogica-ar/baselogica-open-addons/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/baselogica-ar/baselogica-open-addons/issues/new?body=module:%20sale_exception_order_restrictions_bl%0Aversion:%2020.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20...%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical issues.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"-------\n"
"\n"
"* Base Lógica\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"- `Base Lógica <https://baselogica.com>`__\n"
"\n"
"Maintainers\n"
"-----------\n"
"\n"
